1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:04,800
Have your injuries improved
any, Avdol? They have.

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,380
As relieved as I am.

3
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:09,277
I'm even more relieved
knowing you're alright.

4
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:13,237
Yes, well, I'm fortunate there was
no significant damage to my cornea.

5
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,457
I'm expected to make a full recovery.

6
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:17,437
This takes me back to middle school.

7
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,657
During what should have
been an ordinary game,

8
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:22,357
one of my classmates took
a baseball to the eye.

9
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,322
He was good as new the next day.

10
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,677
And as it turned out, his eye
had only lost a bit of fluid.

11
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:29,054
Wait, are you serious?

12
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:30,510
No.

13
00:00:30,593 --> 00:00:34,965
I'll get these bandages off in no time,
and I'll catch up with you in a few days.

14
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,700
In 800 kilometers are Cairo and Dio.

15
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,220
Everyone, you must remain vigilant.

16
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:44,577
Now let's see.

17
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:48,057
What kind of language is this
hospital bill written in anyway?

18
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:52,477
I guess it's supposed to be Arabic,
but man, if this crap isn't confusing.

19
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:56,337
The zero is a five, the decimal
is a zero, and the seven is a six.

20
00:00:56,420 --> 00:01:00,237
And what the heck is this wormy-looking
thingamajig supposed to be?

21
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,577
It's a four, so the amount we owe is...

22
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:05,480
46,350 Egyptian pounds!

23
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:06,420
That's insane!

24
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,840
Oh, my God!

25
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:10,900
What kind of dog is he?

26
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:11,830
He's so funny looking.

27
00:01:11,913 --> 00:01:12,743
Look at that.

28
00:01:12,826 --> 00:01:14,277
Why in the world is he chewing gum?

29
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:16,184
He must be waiting for someone.

30
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:17,931
Such a good little doggy.

31
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:20,937
And here I thought Iggy
was waiting for us outside.

32
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:21,850
Good grief.

33
00:01:21,933 --> 00:01:23,537
Looks like he's a hit with the ladies.

34
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:26,057
Should we tell him doggies
don't usually chew gum?

35
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:28,000
What a peculiar little puppy.

36
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,257
Hello there, ladies.

37
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:30,170
Hmm?

38
00:01:30,253 --> 00:01:32,477
Here's a little bit of
friendly advice for you girls.

39
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:34,417
Step away if you know what's good for you.

40
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,497
I know he comes across as a
charming furball at first,

41
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:40,757
but deep in his soul, he harbors
an extreme hatred for people.

42
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,546
If you're not careful
when you least expect...

43
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,537
What the hell are you doing?!

44
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:47,326
Get off of me, you damn mutt!

45
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,860
You're such a beauty!

46
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:53,857
Oh, you get along so well!

47
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:56,397
In your dreams, we don't get along at all.

48
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,310
Damn it, Iggy.

49
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,757
Would you get the hell off of me?

50
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,257
We'll catch you guys later.

51
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:01,820
See you, lovebirds. Mr.

52
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,317
Joestar, please help me.

53
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,341
Hey, hang on a minute, would you?

54
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,100
What the hell?

55
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:11,200
You nasty little mutt!

56
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:41,360
I don't know.

57
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:55,175
The end of the world.

58
00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:58,380
Stop it now!

59
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:03,477
It's the end of the world.

60
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,697
It's the end of the world.

61
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:08,060
I'm going to continue to walk.

62
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,437
The end of the world.

63
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:15,040
I'm going to go to the last page.

64
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:22,120
I'm going to go to the end of the world.

65
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,760
In ancient times,

66
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:47,597
Egyptians were in the habit of burying
their dead on the west bank of?

67
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,327
the Nile where the sun sets.

68
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:53,597
That's the reason Egyptian cities
stand on the east side of the Nile.

69
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,209
On the west side, however,

70
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:59,422
you're likely to find graves and
mortuary temples scattered about.

71
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,426
But our enemies don't
care about east or west.

72
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:05,952
They'll come from whatever
direction is most advantageous.

73
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:15,120
Look, I know you didn't ask for my opinion,
but your cows are far too lethargic.

74
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:17,907
Although they're strong,
I'll give them that.

75
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,360
Hey, Chaka!

76
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:20,738
Move your ass, boy!

77
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:23,587
And would you stop
dragging the rear already?

78
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:26,660
What a disgrace!

79
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:27,940
Some man you are!

80
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,680
How are you, my son?

81
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:34,692
Looks like your son and your
cow have something in common.

82
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:42,337
A sword?

83
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,877
What's something like this doing out here?

84
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:45,790
Hey, look!

85
00:04:45,873 --> 00:04:47,680
It's a sword! Give me that!

86
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,380
Look at that.

87
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,597
Must have been dropped.

88
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,957
I can't believe no one's
come back to claim it.

89
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:56,617
Their loss is our gain, because this
sword is probably worth a fortune.

90
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:59,229
Hey, what if the owner's
still in the area?

91
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,797
Poor guy must be
panicking right about now.

92
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:04,777
On the off chance it's some
kind of fancy-schmancy artifact,

93
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:06,117
shouldn't we give it to the police?

94
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,030
You idiot!

95
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:10,317
This sword could be the end
of all of our money troubles!

96
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,117
But I'm the one who found it.

97
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,637
It won't be worth a damn
thing if it's blunt.

98
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,257
Pull it out so we can take a look.

99
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:17,170
Right.

100
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,870
What's wrong?

101
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,940
The damn thing won't budge.

102
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,924
Why the hell won't it come out?

103
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:27,940
That's weird.

104
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:29,540
Let me try it. Take it.

105
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,320
You hold this end. Right.

106
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:40,260
It's no use.

107
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,917
The blade hasn't moved
a single centimeter.

108
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,580
Father, let me have a go.

109
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,130
Oh, shut up!

110
00:05:46,213 --> 00:05:49,729
If I can't free it, what chance
does an idiot like you have?

111
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:51,740
My hands!

112
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:53,531
What happened to my hand?

113
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:56,800
My hand!

114
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,600
Why is it spewing blood?

115
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:02,057
How the hell did the sword cut me?

116
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:05,077
We pulled on a damn thing, but
the blade wouldn't come out.

117
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,957
All I did was grab it by the hill.

118
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,037
There's something
strange about that sword.

119
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,885
Hey, you think now's a
good time for me to try?

120
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:12,810
You know what?

121
00:06:12,893 --> 00:06:13,723
Fine.

122
00:06:13,806 --> 00:06:15,162
Go ahead and try it if you want.

123
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,000
It came out so easy.

124
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:32,482
I didn't put the slightest
bit of effort into it.

125
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:34,490
What?

126
00:06:34,573 --> 00:06:35,403
I can hear it.

127
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,160
This makes no sense.

128
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:39,460
I can hear the blade ringing.

129
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,717
I'm by no means an expert when it comes
to swords or things of that nature.

130
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:48,737
But I don't think I've ever
encountered a blade this beautiful.

131
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,637
It's like a rare Japanese katana.

132
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:53,197
It glistens like it's
cloaked in ice-cold water.

133
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,777
We've been graced with
an amazing discovery.

134
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:56,937
Hand it over, my boy!

135
00:06:57,020 --> 00:06:57,997
I don't like you!

136
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:01,198
It has no business wielding
such a valuable treasure!

137
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,920
Oh, God! Sugar!

138
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:07,450
Why?

139
00:07:07,533 --> 00:07:10,200
Why would you do this to your father?

140
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:12,697
I don't know what happens.

141
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:15,337
You were standing behind me,
and before I knew it, the sword!

142
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,060
It's not my fault, I swear!

143
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:18,857
Why are you just standing there?

144
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:22,587
We have to hurry and get him to
a doctor before it's too late!

145
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,760
This sword is evil!

146
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:32,276
It's almost as though the
blade has a mind of its own!

147
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:38,080
Be calm.

148
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,580
Still your heart, Chaka.

149
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:44,677
Their deaths mean nothing.

150
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,720
Nothing whatsoever, Chaka.

151
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:48,910
Just...

152
00:07:48,993 --> 00:07:49,920
just who are you?

153
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:53,380
I can't see you, but
I can hear your voice.

154
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:58,860
I am the stand of the god
Anubis, ruler of the underworld,

155
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:02,020
deity of embalming, and lord of the dead.

156
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:07,180
You have unsheathed me, thus
you shall be my standings.

157
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:11,620
You are a virtuoso, so I shall
make you master of the world.

158
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:15,317
You shall wield me, and you shall kill.

159
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,753
Kill, kill, kill, kill.

160
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:24,517
Father and that man deserve to die, so
they should be thrilled that I killed them.

161
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,357
I think I'll hack you to
pieces while I'm on a roll.

162
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,497
Wait a minute, Chaka!

163
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:30,377
You don't really want to do this!

164
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:31,417
Please let me live, okay?

165
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,760
I don't want to die!

166
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:39,660
How the hell did he do that?

167
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,635
Somehow the cow's completely unharmed!

168
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:58,020
Slaughter Joseph, slice
Polnareff, cleave Jotaro in two.

169
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:02,460
You are a fighting genius,
a master of the sword.

170
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:05,586
No one in the world is
a match for your blade.

171
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:06,680
No one!

172
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:11,140
Come, Ambo.

173
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:15,226
Come on, do we really have time
to lounge around in this place?

174
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,757
Would you quit complaining?

175
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:19,517
They've been kind enough to
allow us passage on their ferry,

176
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,247
so we must show our respect.

177
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:25,717
I don't know about you guys, but I'm
starving, so let's get something to eat.

178
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,447
Wow, you never stop, do you?

179
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:30,077
Here, this should tide you over for now.

180
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:32,057
You know damn well that's eggies!

181
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:34,258
Would you just take the gum already?

182
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,104
Hey, where's the bathroom, huh?

183
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,555
Shall we look for it?

184
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:41,400
Hey, mister, over here!

185
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:43,357
Wanna buy some papyrus?

186
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,740
This papyrus is the original paper.

187
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:47,597
Want a piece of Egyptian history?

188
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:48,577
Here, take a look.

189
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:51,940
This is 100 % Bone Feet
papyrus. Papyrus, huh?

190
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:53,737
I'll give you a good price.

191
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:56,077
Are you positive this is the real thing?

192
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,157
Of course, my friend.

193
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:01,946
I'll have you know a famous Egyptian
craftsman drew this, so it's quite genuine.

194
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,640
This crap is fake and you know it.

195
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:09,517
If this were actual papyrus,
it wouldn't rip so easily.

196
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,460
I'm no fool.

197
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,550
You should try a little.

198
00:10:11,633 --> 00:10:13,500
For the love of, where'd Mr.

199
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:15,149
Joestar and the others go?

200
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,280
Not was that Iggy?

201
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:24,240
Why, you get back here, you little butt!

202
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,240
Hey, what about my body?

203
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:33,480
Stupid dog.

204
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:35,160
He managed to get away.

205
00:11:14,620 --> 00:11:19,780
Gotta say, if my hunch is correct, then
you've got a lot of balls, my friend.

206
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:22,017
Seems like you're planning to attack me

207
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:24,637
while we're in a crowd
of innocent bystanders.

208
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:26,800
Guys like you are a rare breed.

209
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:31,965
Stand users don't usually show themselves,
let alone face their attacker head-on.

210
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,820
It's kind of noble.

211
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:36,614
I didn't think you guys had that trait.

212
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:38,200
Tell me your name.

213
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:45,000
My name is Chaka,

214
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:49,440
and my stand is known as Anubis, the
one true ruler of the Underworld.

215
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:55,080
Now then, Jean-Pierre Polnareff,
prepare to surrender your life to me.

216
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:58,641
You want me to surrender my life?

217
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:01,977
Man, oh man, you sure don't
mince words, do you, Chaka?

218
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:06,707
If nothing else, your confidence is more
impressive than your other companions.

219
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:16,000
Give me your best shot.

220
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:19,829
Let's see if your Anubis stand
is all it's cracked up to be.

221
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:33,680
Come out, chariot!

222
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,520
He's brandishing his sword,

223
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:44,719
but is he really planning to fight
me with that instead of his stand?

224
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,781
Something's off.

225
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:59,980
His movements, his grip, his stance,
they're the dead giveaways of an amateur.

226
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:01,907
But that doesn't make sense.

227
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:04,580
I need to keep my distance from him!

228
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:29,457
What the hell is going on here?

229
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:32,797
His sword passed right
through the pillar and if

230
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,517
that wasn't enough he got
me without leaving even a

231
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:38,897
single tear in my shirt if
I hadn't stepped back when

232
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:43,540
I did I would have been
killed you bastard cheerios

233
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:52,500
damn it why don't you show yourself and
face me like a real fighter you coward

234
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:09,830
Merd.

235
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,720
This can't be happening.

236
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,060
I lost him.

237
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:16,380
He could be hiding behind
any one of these pillars.

238
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:20,437
Judging from his attacks, his sword
can pass through solid objects.

239
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:25,077
And unfortunately for me, my chariot's
striking range is only about one meter.

240
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:25,990
Damn it.

241
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:27,497
He's tougher than I thought he'd be.

242
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:30,297
I honestly can't believe
this asshole is actually

243
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:33,057
giving me a run for my
money in a sword fight.

244
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:36,880
But mark my words, you won't
have the upper hand for long.

245
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,166
Hey Chaka, are you listening?

246
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:44,157
I've got a nice fuse, so
let's see what you've got.

247
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,377
There's no way you can sneak up
on me if I'm not behind a pillar.

248
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:49,737
Unless you're planning on
popping out of the ground.

249
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:51,300
Ha ha ha!

250
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:03,940
What the…

251
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:06,320
He's behind the pillar!

252
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:08,877
My sword doesn't need
to pass through objects!

253
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:12,784
With the power of this blade I
can cut through the pillar itself!

254
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,600
Now die, Pondarest!

255
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:35,320
Man, that was a close one.

256
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:39,797
That technique is so secret that
not even Jotaro knows about it.

257
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:42,056
Silver Chariot can launch its rapier.

258
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:44,680
The downside is I only get one shot.

259
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,857
My opponent dodges I'm history.

260
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:49,980
A last resort once I've
exhausted my other options.

261
00:15:52,420 --> 00:15:54,420
While it's true I didn't kill you,

262
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:58,151
I highly doubt you'll be getting
back up for another round.

263
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,330
Huh?

264
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:03,780
That's peculiar.

265
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,700
How the heck did it get
back into its scabbard?

266
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:11,600
Did it slip in by chance?

267
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:27,640
I didn't notice before,

268
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:32,980
but now that I see it up close, I
fully appreciate the sword's beauty.

269
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:35,260
I have to unsheathe it.

270
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:43,720
Hey there, Polnareff.

271
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:44,737
Thought we'd lost you.

272
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:47,597
We were worried when you up
and vanished by yourself.

273
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,268
We thought you'd been
ambushed by the enemy.

274
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:55,580
Wait, are you okay?

275
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:57,250
Huh?

276
00:16:57,333 --> 00:16:59,700
Oh, it's you, Mr. Joestar.

277
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,296
I'm so fuzzy, I can't think straight.

278
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:04,257
Maybe it's from being tossed around.

279
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:06,516
My injuries are worse than I thought.

280
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,777
Polnareff, why are you
squatting like that?

281
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:14,801
You didn't step in poop, did you?

282
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,577
Polnareff, how did you
come across that sword?

283
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:20,425
Did something happen out here?

284
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:24,057
Yeah, I had a showdown with
some dirtbag that attacked me.

285
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:24,970
What?

286
00:17:25,053 --> 00:17:25,883
An enemy stand user?

287
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:27,297
It's all over now.

288
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:30,086
He said his stand was
known as the god Anubis.

289
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:33,877
It was able to literally
phase through objects and

290
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:36,777
cut them once it had a
target in its crosshairs.

291
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:38,457
He was a strong foe.

292
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:42,180
But despite his formidable power,
when all was said and done,

293
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:46,137
he was no match for the likes of
me, Polnareff reassured himself.

294
00:17:46,220 --> 00:17:48,280
He was using this sword as his way.

295
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,340
Where did it go?

296
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:52,917
Where'd those rats come from?

297
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,717
And why are they making off of the sword?

298
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:55,741
Get out of here!

299
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,840
Jeez, talk about creepy.

300
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:02,915
No one told me even the rats
steal stuff in this place.

301
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:06,935
If you guys want to steal
something, steal some cheese.

302
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:11,117
Yeah that's unusual.

303
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:13,597
The sword stuck in the scabbard.

304
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:15,477
It's jammed in here really tight.

305
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:17,157
Hey Polnareff.

306
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:21,137
While I'm relieved that you're all right,
don't ever run off by yourself again.

307
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:22,050
Got it.

308
00:18:22,133 --> 00:18:22,963
It's dangerous.

309
00:18:23,046 --> 00:18:26,877
The enemy will find a way to attack you
even if you're just alone for a few seconds.

310
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:30,977
Oh crap. I forgot.

311
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:33,037
That's the sound of our ship taking off.

312
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:35,237
Without us, we need to
hurry and get on board.

313
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,150
We're

314
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:45,617
heading to Edfa today.

315
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:46,530
What?

316
00:18:46,613 --> 00:18:47,697
Come on guys, wait for me.

317
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:51,177
Polnareff, so you decided to bring
the sword with you after all.

318
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:53,537
Yeah, I'm gonna turn it in to the police.

319
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:55,737
This thing is a dangerous
weapon, you know.

320
00:18:55,820 --> 00:18:57,280
Hmm, that's a good plan.

321
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,957
Anyone could pick it up at those
ruins, so we can't take any chances.

322
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:03,158
It's probably worth a small fortune.

323
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:09,980
Quiet, Iggy.

324
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,417
You can't make noise in here.

325
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:14,029
If you keep this up,
we can get kicked out.

326
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:17,797
What the hell is wrong
with that mutt today?

327
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:20,277
Ah, well, since the
damn dog won't shut up,

328
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,242
I guess I'll just take
the sword to the cops now.

329
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:24,337
Polnareff, weren't you?

330
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:26,197
listening when we told you not to go off!

331
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,110
on your own?

332
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:29,617
Seriously, we talked about this earlier.

333
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:32,597
Jotaro, tag along and keep
him out of trouble, would ya?

334
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:33,510
Gotcha.

335
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:48,597
Hey, shouldn't our first stop
have been the police station?

336
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,560
Oh, take it easy, Jotaro.

337
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:53,997
A man's got to look his absolute
best, as the saying goes.

338
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:55,480
Oh, before I forget.

339
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:59,337
Old man, you mind putting this
over there out of the way?

340
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:00,250
Sure.

341
00:20:00,333 --> 00:20:01,922
That thing's a dangerous weapon.

342
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:04,977
All right, back to what
I was saying earlier.

343
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:08,597
I did a fair amount of rolling around
and ended up getting kind of dirty.

344
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:12,220
Make this face gorgeous
again, Mr. Barber. Will do.

345
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:14,570
Ow!

346
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:15,730
Ow!

347
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,312
Hey, would you watch it?

348
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:19,917
In case you haven't
noticed, that razor's dull.

349
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:20,830
Come on, Mr.

350
00:20:20,913 --> 00:20:22,257
Barber, sharpen that thing.

351
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:25,928
This is supposed to be the most
relaxing part of the haircut.

352
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:28,917
Good grief, you're such a prima donna.

353
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,500
You're right sir.

354
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:32,120
My apologies

355
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:13,017
Oh, better.

356
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:13,960
Much better.

357
00:21:14,220 --> 00:21:15,573
Now that's a shave, Mr.

358
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:16,530
Barber.

359
00:21:16,613 --> 00:21:17,905
That's what I'm talking about.

360
00:21:18,460 --> 00:21:19,290
Thank you.

361
00:21:19,373 --> 00:21:21,000
I'm glad to hear it.

362
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:23,160
Tre Bone, barber.

363
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:24,720
Tre Bone, man.

364
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:27,817
And now, if you wouldn't
mind getting under my chin.

365
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:28,730
Sure.

366
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:30,800
Right here.

367
00:21:31,780 --> 00:21:34,120
Under your chin, yes. Huh?

368
00:21:38,300 --> 00:21:41,280
You did say under your
chin, right, Polnareff?

369
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:42,580
What the hell?

370
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,460
Remember me, you fool?

371
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:48,858
I'm the Anubistan, and this
time you're going to die!

372
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:58,400
Thank you.

373
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:30,020
Thank you.

374
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:25,040
The sword is the stand!

375
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:27,677
I won't lose twice to the same adversary.

376
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:28,819
This guy's strong.

377
00:23:28,940 --> 00:23:31,697
The more we fight this
stand, the faster it gets.

378
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:33,240
His eyes that stare.

379
00:23:33,500 --> 00:23:35,720
This time, I'll take your head!
